<title>MEXICO: Mexico 28-day Cetes rate falls 102 bps in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico 28-day Cetes rate falls 102 bps in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose slightly, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	17.70	    -102	    17.60     17.74</p>
<p>91-Day	19.00	    - 67	    18.90     19.10</p>
<p>182-Day     20.25	    - 38	    20.10     20.30</p>
<p>364-Day     20.24				20.19     20.35</p>
<p>Last week the 343-day paper was assigned at 20.83 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.24 bln pesos    2.81</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   3.49 bln pesos    4.37</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   3.08 bln pesos    3.85</p>
<p>364-Day     600 million pesos   1.50 bln pesos    2.49</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.44 on demand of 10.31 billion pesos compared with 3.36 the week before on demand of 10.08 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    4 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   10 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   5 basis points</p>
<p>    364-Day			  11 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
</text>
